<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-MIDI LIBRE FIRST STAGE PLACINGS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-MIDI LIBRE FIRST STAGE PLACINGS.</headline>
<dateline>BARAQUEVILLE, France 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in</p>
<p>the 199-km first stage of the Midi Libre cycle race over from</p>
<p>Narbonne on Tuesday:</p>
<p> 1. Laurent Desbiens (France) Cofidis	5 hours 23 minutes</p>
<p> 2. Bo Hanburger (Denmark) TVM		   8 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Luca Gelfi (Italy) Brescialat			12 seconds</p>
<p>4. Rodolfo Massi (Italy) Casino</p>
<p>5. Jan Ullrich (Germany) Telekom</p>
<p>6. Cedric Vasseur (France) Gan</p>
<p>7. Dariusz Baranowski (Poland) US Postal Service</p>
<p>8. Angel Casero-Moreno (Spain) Banesto</p>
<p>9. Joona Laukka (Finland) Festina</p>
<p> 10 Stephane Petilleau (France) TVM	    all same time as</p>
<p>Gelfi</p>
<p>Leading overall standings:</p>
<p> 1. Desbiens			  5 hours 22 minutes 50 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Hamburger					 12 seconds behind</p>
<p> 3. Gelfi							18 seconds</p>
<p> 4. Baranowski						 21</p>
<p> 5. Massi							22</p>
<p>6. Ullrich</p>
<p>7. Vasseur</p>
<p>8. Casero-Moreno</p>
<p> 9. Laukka 10. Petilleau		   all same time as Massi</p>
</text>
